Add the @nswds/tokens token layers to your Tailwind entry CSS (after `@import "tailwindcss";`):

@import "@nswds/tokens/tailwind/preset.css";
@import "@nswds/tokens/css/colors/global/oklch.css";
@import "@nswds/tokens/css/colors/semantic/oklch.css";
@import "@nswds/tokens/css/colors/semantic/oklch.dark.css";
@import "@nswds/tokens/css/colors/themes/masterbrand/oklch.css";
@import "@nswds/tokens/tailwind/colors/themes/masterbrand/oklch.css";

`preset.css` wires every token category (colour, radius, space, typography, motion, shadow, border) into Tailwind in a single import. Keep the oklch colour layers AFTER it so the palette stays oklch (preset bundles hex values); the masterbrand layers add the brand theme, which preset excludes. The semantic DARK layer is scoped `.dark`, so the role tokens these variables map onto flip automatically — toggle the `.dark` class on your root element for dark mode (no separate dark variable block needed).

See https://github.com/digitalnsw/nswds-ui/blob/main/docs/installing-from-the-registry.md
